  "articleBodyHtml": "<h2>The Value of the Creative Process</h2>\n<p>It&#x27;s important to enjoy the process of creating and receiving feedback. The act of putting something out there and being appraised by others can be a rewarding experience. Many artists find joy in the journey of creation, rather than focusing solely on the outcome. This mindset allows for personal growth and deeper engagement with one&#x27;s work.</p>\n<p>Different people have different goals when creating art. Some may be driven by a desire for personal expression, while others may seek validation or recognition. These varying motivations shape the artistic journey and influence how artists approach their work.</p>\n<p>Seeking validation through likes and recognition can be a motivating factor for artists. Many artists rely on external feedback to feel encouraged and to measure the impact of their work. However, this can also lead to self-doubt if recognition is not received as expected.</p>\n<p>Artists often desire recognition and validation from others. This desire can be both a source of motivation and a potential source of frustration. When artists do not receive the recognition they seek, it can lead to feelings of inadequacy and a loss of confidence in their abilities.</p>\n<p>Artists can experience self-doubt and frustration when they don&#x27;t receive recognition for their work. This emotional struggle is common among many artists, especially those who rely heavily on external validation to feel successful in their craft.</p>\n<h2>記事情報</h2>\n<p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7SbwN9k_NjQ</p>",
